{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance","id":1549633,"title":"Cloaking Resonance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-03-29T09:07:05-07:00","id":1549633,"title":"Cloaking Resonance","content":"Concealing/changing one's aura is a Prime 2 effect, according to M20.<br /> <br /> Book of the Fallen has a rote to conceal aura and resonance. Weirdly, in this rote, to conceal your Resonance you don't roll Arete, but Willpower at diff of Resonance trait+3 and you need 1 success per Resonance point. It last for 1 hour per success. <br /> <br /> In Book of Secrets, this same rule applies, but not in a rote. It seems every mage can do that &quot;by asserting a degree of control over the manifestation&quot;.<br /> So, concealing Resonance requires Prime or not?<br /> <br /> Also, is my understanding, from reading the Resonance chapter of Book of Secrets, that a mage's spells ripples and Resonance are a reflection from their own Resonance trait, which means that by concealing their own Resonance, their spells are also concealed. The example of Jinx in Identifying Signatures text (BoS) gives the hint, as so many others through BoS and M20.<br /> <br /> If my understanding is incorrect, how could nephandi cast spells without nearby mages (or other senaitive beings/people) catching all that Jhor and evil/death/etc Resonance?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-05T18:28:06-07:00","id":1549855,"title":"","content":"Resonance is one of the elements of the game that is at the same time central to the game, but <b>very </b>poorly described through mechanics. The rules on Resonance are few and incoherent.<br /> <br /> More importantly, your last question is one the game tries to answer since always without throwing Resonance out of the bath. It wants to have the cake and eat it too.<br /> <br /> At the end, you have options. Don't try to find a definitive, canon answer (just as you shouldn't for Paradox, but even more so here). Take those you think better fit within your current chronicle.<br /> <br /> If you want to have Nefandi being a hidden threat, they should have access to a means to obscure their resonance. How exactly this means works, on the other hand, depends on how easy you want for <i>other</i> Mages to access such means.<br /> <br /> Using Willpower instead of Arete is a means to have low Arete Mages conceal their resonance reliably without the need to make them more powerful. If concealment is a general rule, then that says a lot about what Resonance is and how much control Mages have over their manifestations. Using Resonance instead of Sphere as the basis for the diff makes it so characters that keep their Resonance from increasing get an easier time concealing it, which makes sense, but takes a little from the idea that doing the concealment is an act of Magic by itself. Rotes also have the advantage that the Storyteller can gatekeep them within one faction or another, or at least base them on personal Paradigm.<br /> <br /> No answer here is the correct one, take what you need to run your game. And if you're playing, ask the ST how they run Resonance and Resonance concealment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T16:26:16-07:00","id":1549884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549855#post1549855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to have Nefandi being a hidden threat, they should have access to a means to obscure their resonance. How exactly this means works, on the other hand, depends on how easy you want for <i>other</i> Mages to access such means.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I'm not only thinking about nephandi (they were just the obvious example), but any mage that wants to cloak their magick. I'll explain better later in this post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549855#post1549855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Willpower instead of Arete is a means to have low Arete Mages conceal their resonance reliably without the need to make them more powerful. If concealment is a general rule, then that says a lot about what Resonance is and how much control Mages have over their manifestations. Using Resonance instead of Sphere as the basis for the diff makes it so characters that keep their Resonance from increasing get an easier time concealing it, which makes sense, but takes a little from the idea that doing the concealment is an act of Magic by itself. Rotes also have the advantage that the Storyteller can gatekeep them within one faction or another, or at least base them on personal Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Book of Secrets (p.135) &quot;Cloaking Resonance&quot; is not a rote nor an act of magick, technically. It is described as <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Story-wise, a mage can cloak her Resonance simply by asserting a degree of control over the manifestations. </div> </div> </div>And Book of the Fallen has it inside the rote &quot;Shroud the Soul&quot;, which conceals the nephandi aura and Resonance and requires Mind and Prime (although Prime alone could do both).<br /> <br /> Re-reading the rote description, one thing that came to my mind is that maybe the Nephandi <b>needs</b> a rote and the use of magick, because of their absurdly tainted and corrupted Resonance, and thus the default mode from the BoS isn't enough. That's the only explanation I could think until now.<br /> <br /> Having said that, we know that any non-nephandi mage can reliably cloak their Resonance, but does that mean that their spells are also cloaked?<br /> <br /> For example, if you cast an invisible and coincident effect, like mind reading, could someone with Awareness detect and know what you are doing? What about someone with Prime?<br /> <br /> Even worst, what if you are using invisibility magick, could any Night-Folk, mage, crat just roll Awareness to blow your cover?<br /> <br /> Vampires with Obfuscate, for example, won't be detected unless somone has Auspex <b>and</b> rolls Awareness. Chimeristry is also only broken by Auspex iirc. <br /> <br /> So, it is my understanding that mages should have means of concealing their spells, which leads to two questions which I'd like to get opinions:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Does cloaking Resonance cloaks spells completely? <br /> \u2022 If not, what could do that? A Prime 2 effect?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-06T18:31:30-07:00","id":1549887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549884#post1549884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Does cloaking Resonance cloaks spells completely?<br /> \u2022 If not, what could do that? A Prime 2 effect?</div> </div> </div> </div>Cloaking resonance shouldn't cloak spells completely.<br /> <br /> There are 4 ways to perceive a spell in some manner: its casting method, its direct effects, its Resonance and through magic (in general, be it Awakened Magic or any other supernatural means to detect spells).<br /> <br /> When you cloak Resonance you only obscure that aspect of the spell. It will take away the Mage's signature, along with whatever relevant information it may include. Resonance is generally subtle, but characters with Awareness can notice it. Very strong Resonance is readily visible for anyone, although possibly inexplicable. By itself Resonance tells more about how a spell came to be and the Mage that made it than what the spell itself actually is or does.<br /> <br /> So Resonance alone would give away that a spell was cast or a Mage is nearby, but about the spell itself it wouldn't tell much more than this. Resonance effects are perceptible in the general vicinity of an invisible target, but they don't give away the actual target's location, or even that it is an invisibility spell.<br /> <br /> Mages trying to cloak their presence and works should certainly consider cloaking their Resonance, if this is at all possible, but their spells won't fail completely to conceal things just because their Resonance isn't cloaked.<br /> <br /> Nefandi have always been the game's focus on means to cloak Resonance because they're meant to be a concealed threat, but their Resonance is a dead giveaway. That's why the game has more word-count on rotes for them to do it than for anyone else.<br /> <br /> For cloaking the spell itself I think Prime 2 would be enough, but it would require quite some successes. At least as much as the spell has in its primary intensity factor should be also in cloaking it. This would preferably be woven into the casting of the spell, otherwise the cloaking effect would need a cloaking itself. Even then, it may be hard to define what cloaking a spell actually entails. Is a cloaked portal invisible to Correspondence, even if it is literally a hole in space?<br /> <br /> I'm unsure if cloaking spells in this sense should be a thing in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T08:51:08-07:00","id":1549909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549887#post1549887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cloaking resonance shouldn't cloak spells completely.<br /> <br /> There are 4 ways to perceive a spell in some manner: its casting method, its direct effects, its Resonance and through magic (in general, be it Awakened Magic or any other supernatural means to detect spells).</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by casting method? Like instruments?<br /> <br /> Its direct effect might not be noticeable, like the mind reading example (and so many others).<br /> <br /> Resonance can be cloaked, as we discussed before, which leads us to the last one in your list: through magic. I believe this one means things like Prime, Auspex and any kind of Gift that allows garou to sense magick.<br /> I'm ok with nightfolk that has spend time and resources into a power that allows them to track down supernatural things being able to <b> try</b> (with some resisted roll) and track the use of magick. My issue is with basically [b]any[b/] foe (including True Faith mortals) being able to detect magick without a resisted roll.<br /> <br /> The way Obfuscation works, to me, seems to be the ideal way. The target needs some sort of supernatural power (Auspex) and a roll (or not be able to see at all if Obfuscate &gt; Auspex).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549887#post1549887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you cloak Resonance you only obscure that aspect of the spell. It will take away the Mage's signature, along with whatever relevant information it may include. Resonance is generally subtle, but characters with Awareness can notice it. Very strong Resonance is readily visible for anyone, although possibly inexplicable. By itself Resonance tells more about how a spell came to be and the Mage that made it than what the spell itself actually is or does.<br /> So Resonance alone would give away that a spell was cast or a Mage is nearby, but about the spell itself it wouldn't tell much more than this. Resonance effects are perceptible in the general vicinity of an invisible target, but they don't give away the actual target's location, or even that it is an invisibility spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. Resonance is only slightly (if ever) affected by what the spell does. Probably only in very powerful spells, with very strong Resonances.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549887#post1549887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Mages trying to cloak their presence and works should certainly consider cloaking their Resonance, if this is at all possible, but their spells won't fail completely to conceal things just because their Resonance isn't cloaked.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the issue, what exactly have to be cloaked so Night-Folks and True Faith mortals cannot sense a spell being cast? Everywhere I read, Resonance seems to be the thing that can be sensed and gives the spell away.<br /> <br /> M20 has some description in p.358<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The uncanny currents of Quintessence, Resonance, Synergy,<br /> Nodes, gateways, and other paranormal phenomena have sensory<br /> effects as well. Most mages can sense energy and determine its<br /> flavor even when there\u2019s no physical contact involved. Strong<br /> Resonance and Synergy cast impressions that sensitive characters<br /> can perceive and potentially read. One location might ripple with<br /> corruption even when the sun shines on its apparently peaceful<br /> ground; another could hold a calming sense of peace that soothes<br /> a troubled soul in the middle of a storm.<br /> Magickal workings can ripple the environment as well,<br /> especially when the Correspondence, Entropy, Forces, Spirit,<br /> and Time Spheres are involved. Mages who understand those<br /> Spheres stand a pretty decent chance of sensing familiar magicks\u2026<br /> which can, in turn, warn your heroes (or their enemies!) of some<br /> impending spell. Let\u2019s say that Nix has a few dots in the Time<br /> Sphere; a faint breeze that smells like the past and future shaking<br /> hands could alert Nix to the presence of a rival mage who\u2019s using<br /> temporal magicks to attack Nix by surprise. In game terms, you<br /> can offer a vague description and see if your player gets the hint;<br /> if so, let him roll Perception + Alertness\u2026 and if he succeeds, let<br /> him catch sight of the magick before it strikes.\u200b </div> </div> </div>I believe Alertness is wrong here and they meant Awareness. Still, the description of how mages can sense seems to fall only in Resonance, Quintessence (which might not always be used, unless you consider Tapestry quintessence, which could be a good argument) and Synergy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549887#post1549887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b\u200b<br /> For cloaking the spell itself I think Prime 2 would be enough, but it would require quite some successes. At least as much as the spell has in its primary intensity factor should be also in cloaking it. This would preferably be woven into the casting of the spell, otherwise the cloaking effect would need a cloaking itself. Even then, it may be hard to define what cloaking a spell actually entails. Is a cloaked portal invisible to Correspondence, even if it is literally a hole in space?<br /> <br /> I'm unsure if cloaking spells in this sense should be a thing in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see three ways of doing that: casting a spell and then cloaking it with Prime (and as you said, the Prime 2 spell cloaked as well); casting an already cloaked spell with Prime (although that would probably require more successes than the original spell) or casting a Prime cloaking effect locked in your pattern, concealing your magickal doings (but that woul require Prime 2 + Life 2, for locking).<br /> <br /> In your portal example, I'd say that the &quot;Tapestry manipulation&quot; of the spell is cloaked, but the effect of the spell isn't (the &quot;direct effects&quot; that you talked about before). This means that scaning the portal with Awareness or Prime wouldn't point to a magickal effect, like if it was a mundane/natural thing, but a Correspondence scan can point to an abnormality\u200b in space. Obviously, any mage seing the portal would conclude it is magickal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T10:24:20-07:00","id":1549916,"title":"","content":"For cloacking spells...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, if you cast an invisible and coincident effect, like mind reading, could someone with Awareness detect and know what you are doing? What about someone with Prime?<br /> <br /> Even worst, what if you are using invisibility magick, could any Night-Folk, mage, crat just roll Awareness to blow your cover?<br /> <br /> Vampires with Obfuscate, for example, won't be detected unless somone has Auspex <b>and</b> rolls Awareness. Chimeristry is also only broken by Auspex iirc.<br /> <br /> So, it is my understanding that mages should have means of concealing their spells, which leads to two questions which I'd like to get opinions:</div> </div> </div> </div>Before even approaching the idea I think it's worth to think about cloaking from <i>what,</i> and what are the goalposts .<br /> <br /> For instance, I don't think Awareness alone should detect mind reading as much more than &quot;someone it's using magick in the proximity&quot;. To know what it's happening you need other senses. Think that sensing what Spheres are being used to cast a spell used to be a Prime 2 Effect on revised, not even lvl 1, obviously not something you can just detect by default.<br /> <br /> Awareness it's like detecting &quot;a disturbance in the force&quot;, you know there's supernatural shenanigans being done. With a lot of successes you may be able to discern a bit more information, such as the magick being tainted with a dangerous ressonance, but that doesn't mean you can pinpoint <i>exactly </i>where the &quot;effect&quot; is or what it's it's intent.<br /> <br /> And about Invisibility:<br /> <br /> *In the part where seeing trough illusions it's talked about on the Core (the &quot;I Disbelieve&quot; table), Awareness ain't mentioned. It's Willpower to break mental illusions and Alertness to sense flaws in physical illusions.<br /> *On HDYDT it's mentioned a roll of Awareness <i>or </i>Alertness to see trough illusions, but perhaps only if players ask for it specifically (I hate how HDYDT words stuff).<br /> *BoS rescues a <b>5 dots Merit</b> from previous editions that allows to sense illusions with a roll of Awareness with a difficulty dependant on the Sphere level being used (the Merit also works with Obfuscate and other powers), and then says that &quot;if a roll would normally be allowed&quot; it's at -3 diff (to allow the &quot;I Disbelieve&quot; rule to exist, although now sits behind a rather unclear &quot;if&quot;).<br /> <br /> Clearly M20 struggles about what to do with illusions. M20 has a serious issue of trying to make everything resistible or &quot;dodge-able&quot; even when it doesn't make a lot of sense. But around all that mess Awareness breaking illusions seems more of an outlier of &quot;illusions aren't supposed to be perfect, everyone should be able to see trough them&quot; - that clashes with both previous editions where illusions were very much perfect barring non-human senses and special powers (hence why it's worth a 5 dots merit to break them with a Skill roll...) AND with the very intent behind making illusions in the first place (as noted by HDYDT: &quot;It\u2019s the Storyteller\u2019s option to conceal the nature of an illusion from her players \u2013 that usually is the purpose of an illusion, after all!&quot; p.129).<br /> <br /> If Mage it's clashing with itself on this, even &quot;intra edition&quot;, IMAGINE if it's going to be balanced with Obfuscate :P <hr /><br /> As for magick to conceal magick, it seems counter-intuitive to spend more successes, thus making the magick stronger, to make it's trace fainter. That's a struggle that needs to be taken in count. Some ideas:<br /> <br /> *Noise: We know moments where abundant Time magick has been used are harder to scry because of the temporal interference. So I think you could similarly conceal the supernatural within more supernatural. You could conceal a portal generating other spatial disturbances in the area. Prime 2 could be able to move the quintaessential stuff around so much that, yeah, there's a disturbance in the force, but you can't know much more about it - may even cause a sensory overload<br /> <br /> *Cloack of delussion: Taking a page from the No-Mind rote (a glorified &quot;mind shield&quot; that, if undefeated, shows as if the target had nothing in it's mind) and Obfuscate (that works by causing everyone in the area to refuse to acknowledge the vampire). Maybe you could use Mind 3 or 4 to surround your effect with an aura that makes would-be Awareness users in it's AOE think there's &quot;no magick arround&quot;. It's not really hidding the magick, it's trying to subjugate everyone into ignoring it - subject to all the limitations and complications of Mind magick, ofc.<br /> <br /> *Destroying/Blocking the magick?: Not sure if this is possible, and it's entirely dependant on the ST on both it being feasible and what effects exactly it would have. But since Awareness it's specifically called out ... Awareness detects &quot;something&quot;, but AFAIK we don't know how this it's happening (or do we?). Maybe it's an &quot;emanation of power&quot;, or a &quot;vibration of reality being altered&quot;, maybe it's more abstract: See the section about the Periphery, maybe it's supernatural things getting a reflection &quot;beyond the materialistic world&quot;, and people seeing that reflection.<br /> Whatever it's the case, I would imagine a Master mage could know how magick it's being sensed, and try to prevent that from happening. Perhaps you could prevent the magick power from escaping like an inverted faraday cage, &quot;smooth&quot; it's weaves somehow, or destroy any kind of resiudue it produces on another world ... no idea how this would work since IDK the specifics, but, other than Prime, Entropy 5 comes to mind since allows the destruction of some abstract and ephemeral things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-07-2025, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T11:44:59-07:00","id":1549919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549916#post1549916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For cloacking spells...<br /> <br /> Before even approaching the idea I think it's worth to think about cloaking from <i>what,</i> and what are the goalposts .</div> </div> </div> </div>That is exactly my question. What, besides Resonance and Synergy, can be detected by those with supernatural sensing? If you remove Resonance, what trail/disturbance/etc does magick create?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549916#post1549916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, I don't think Awareness alone should detect mind reading as much more than &quot;someone it's using magick in the proximity&quot;. To know what it's happening you need other senses. Think that sensing what Spheres are being used to cast a spell used to be a Prime 2 Effect on revised, not even lvl 1, obviously not something you can just detect by default.<br /> <br /> Awareness it's like detecting &quot;a disturbance in the force&quot;, you know there's supernatural shenanigans being done. With a lot of successes you may be able to discern a bit more information, such as the magick being tainted with a dangerous ressonance, but that doesn't mean you can pinpoint <i>exactly </i>where the &quot;effect&quot; is or what it's it's intent.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is also my take on the talent from all of its descriptions throughout editions, but then M20 uses it to help dodge magick and break illusions (as you pointed out), etc.<br /> <br /> <br /> [QUOTE=Aleph;n1549916]<br /> And about Invisibility:[\\quote]<br /> <br /> To be honest, invisibility was just an example. My issue is with detecting all sorts of magick so easily. If you want to use Forces to push someone from a stair, a mage or nightfolk might scan and see that magick was used. If you give someone a heart attack, the crat can feel magick working and trace to you.<br /> <br /> So, there should be at least a way to hide your effects from other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Which brings to your solutions:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549916#post1549916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for magick to conceal magick, it seems counter-intuitive to spend more successes, thus making the magick stronger, to make it's trace fainter. That's a struggle that needs to be taken in count. Some ideas:<br /> <br /> *Noise: We know moments where abundant Time magick has been used are harder to scry because of the temporal interference. So I think you could similarly conceal the supernatural within more supernatural. You could conceal a portal generating other spatial disturbances in the area. Prime 2 could be able to move the quintaessential stuff around so much that, yeah, there's a disturbance in the force, but you can't know much more about it - may even cause a sensory overload</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this option, but that would probably need to answer that first question: <i>what exactly needs to be concealed (by noise) if not Resonance/Syenergy?</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549916#post1549916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Cloack of delussion: Taking a page from the No-Mind rote (a glorified &quot;mind shield&quot; that, if undefeated, shows as if the target had nothing in it's mind) and Obfuscate (that works by causing everyone in the area to refuse to acknowledge the vampire). Maybe you could use Mind 3 or 4 to surround your effect with an aura that makes would-be Awareness users in it's AOE think there's &quot;no magick arround&quot;. It's not really hidding the magick, it's trying to subjugate everyone into ignoring it - subject to all the limitations and complications of Mind magick, ofc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, Mind could make the target not detect the spell, but only if you cast it before the nightfolk gets close to the effect (or you use something like a locked effect like I said before with Prime).\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549916#post1549916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Destroying/Blocking the magick?: Not sure if this is possible, and it's entirely dependant on the ST on both it being feasible and what effects exactly it would have. But since Awareness it's specifically called out ... Awareness detects &quot;something&quot;, but AFAIK we don't know how this it's happening (or do we?). Maybe it's an &quot;emanation of power&quot;, or a &quot;vibration of reality being altered&quot;, maybe it's more abstract: See the section about the Periphery, maybe it's supernatural things getting a reflection &quot;beyond the materialistic world&quot;, and people seeing that reflection.<br /> Whatever it's the case, I would imagine a Master mage could know how magick it's being sensed, and try to prevent that from happening. Perhaps you could prevent the magick power from escaping like an inverted faraday cage, &quot;smooth&quot; it's weaves somehow, or destroy any kind of resiudue it produces on another world ... no idea how this would work since IDK the specifics, but, other than Prime, Entropy 5 comes to mind since allows the destruction of some abstract and ephemeral things</div> </div> </div> </div>The description in M20's &quot;Metaphysical Sensations&quot; (p.358) text (the one I posted in #5) says <i>&quot;Magickal workings can ripple the environment as well&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Revised have in Prime 1 description: <i>&quot;alert the mage to the bending of the Tapestry&quot;</i>. And Prime 1 detection rote: <i>&quot;detect the weaving of the etheric threads.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> How exactly are those differente from Resonance/Synergy, I don't know.<br /> <br /> But about your post, that is exactly what I have in mind, considering there really is something besides Resonance to cloak. I'd say &quot;smoothening&quot; is the best term for what i have in mind. Something like a filter. I could see VAs or Etherites preventing magick being sensed using etheric active filters with Op Amps,etc. And I believe you meant Prime 2 or Entropy 5? Because any of those could do the task...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-07T14:45:05-07:00","id":1549924,"title":"","content":"What, besides Resonance and Synergy, can be detected by those with supernatural sensing?<br /> <br /> Well, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> mentioned, the effects have what we could call external manifestations. Such as a portal being a warp in space. Even if the portal it's invisible, Corr 1 should sense the warp. An effect invisible to our senses doesn't need to be invisible to other senses.<br /> <br /> As for Prime:<br /> <br /> Resonance and Synergy, as I see them, are like the &quot;taste&quot; of magick. A mage that kills with his magick leaves &quot;bad vives&quot;, a mage that's a devoted healer may leave an aura of caring or nurturing. The difference between the two it's that Synergy it's Triatic, it's has ties to a higger power - perhaps explaining why killing w. magick it's always so bad, there's something wrong with death itself that makes you not want to resonate with it.<br /> <br /> Quintessence typically has a Ressonance, but this can be cleansed or changed - Technocrats typically &quot;sanitize&quot; the ressonance of a Node. The Quintessence stays there at the same levels, however, and Prime 1 can detect that.<br /> <br /> The Tapestry it's everything that exists, at least this side of the Deep Umbra. The etheric threads most assuredly means the weaving of reality. Anti-Magick uses Quintessence to &quot;harden&quot; reality. And all magick it's related to Quintessence to some extent. Even the powers of other splats are often &quot;translated&quot; to it. Not just the Vitae-Tass infamous conversion, but even the Conviction of Hunters can be replenished with Prime + Tass<br /> <br /> Personally, my primary suspect about how &quot;detect magick&quot; works, it's by detecting the movement of Quintessence. Quintessence makes every &quot;thing&quot; in the universe. And the use of magick always alters the flow of quintessence, that's why the &quot;hardening reality&quot; of Anti-Magick works - because something needs to move or shift, something needs to be &quot;not-hard&quot;, to cast spells the way mages do. That's the &quot;weaving of the etheric threads&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now notice how spells are rarely permanent, and those who are can most often be &quot;unwoven&quot;. That tells us there's something unnatural about the state of the &quot;weave&quot;. That's something that can be detected.<br /> <br /> And that causes a problem with any sort of &quot;smoothering&quot; the weave. Doing it for real, it would unweave the magick. Doing it so things &quot;appear&quot; natural it's a contradiction (the effect itself can be dispelled) - at best, you could use this approach to hide the kind of magick that's inside the *field*, to obscure facts about that magick - but not that there's something magickal there<br /> <br /> Now, the smoothering approach could, perhaps, work as a sort of &quot;cleansing&quot; for instant effects. These are 100% natural (turning to ash after being hit by a fireball it's natural :P ), so only remanent ressonance and the act of casting itself are going to delate them as magick, there's no other &quot;residue&quot; (well, apart from the ash).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-07-2025, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T05:44:10-07:00","id":1549938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549924#post1549924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What, besides Resonance and Synergy, can be detected by those with supernatural sensing?<br /> <br /> Well, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> mentioned, the effects have what we could call external manifestations. Such as a portal being a warp in space. Even if the portal it's invisible, Corr 1 should sense the warp. An effect invisible to our senses doesn't need to be invisible to other senses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and I'm ok with that. If all that is left for detection is the effect results, it's up to the mage to disguise it if he wants to go unnoticed. Of course, the portal example isn't a good one. But imagine that a mage creates a fire effect that is disguised/cloaked/whatever with Prime and now doesn't glow as a magickal act anymore. Any supernatural trying to scan for magick wouldn't be able to tell if it's mundane fire or not (maybe a Forces scan, but idk, would have to figure the rules about that).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549924#post1549924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tapestry it's everything that exists, at least this side of the Deep Umbra. The etheric threads most assuredly means the weaving of reality. Anti-Magick uses Quintessence to &quot;harden&quot; reality. And all magick it's related to Quintessence to some extent. Even the powers of other splats are often &quot;translated&quot; to it. Not just the Vitae-Tass infamous conversion, but even the Conviction of Hunters can be replenished with Prime + Tass<br /> <br /> Personally, my primary suspect about how &quot;detect magick&quot; works, it's by detecting the movement of Quintessence. Quintessence makes every &quot;thing&quot; in the universe. And the use of magick always alters the flow of quintessence, that's why the &quot;hardening reality&quot; of Anti-Magick works - because something needs to move or shift, something needs to be &quot;not-hard&quot;, to cast spells the way mages do. That's the &quot;weaving of the etheric threads&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now notice how spells are rarely permanent, and those who are can most often be &quot;unwoven&quot;. That tells us there's something unnatural about the state of the &quot;weave&quot;. That's something that can be detected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really liked that idea. It makes much more sense than just adding something vague and that was never ever talked about in the setting, like &quot;etheric threads&quot;. And it is completely on par with what Quintessence should be in the game. One of M20 descriptions of Quintessence (p.79) talks about it being &quot;That essence fuels the latticework of all Creation&quot;. That is related to the Tapestry, so bending of the Tapestry would definitely involve manipulating Quintessence.<br /> <br /> Revised has an even better description on Tapestry &quot;All things that exist have their own unique pattern, formed from threads of Quintessence into energy, matter and life&quot;. And &quot;The foundation of reality is magic, its forms a result of interwoven threads of Quintessence.&quot;.<br /> <br /> That definitely answers the question to me. The words used (&quot;thread&quot;, &quot;interwoven&quot;) points directly to how the Tapestry is described. Thank you for that good insight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549924#post1549924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that causes a problem with any sort of &quot;smoothering&quot; the weave. Doing it for real, it would unweave the magick. Doing it so things &quot;appear&quot; natural it's a contradiction (the effect itself can be dispelled) - at best, you could use this approach to hide the kind of magick that's inside the *field*, to obscure facts about that magick - but not that there's something magickal there<br /> <br /> Now, the smoothering approach could, perhaps, work as a sort of &quot;cleansing&quot; for instant effects. These are 100% natural (turning to ash after being hit by a fireball it's natural :P ), so only remanent ressonance and the act of casting itself are going to delate them as magick, there's no other &quot;residue&quot; (well, apart from the ash).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. You don't have to uneave a spell to disguise it. &quot;Smoothering&quot;, &quot;filtering&quot;, &quot;cleansing&quot; are all term that lack proper definition inside the game. What you need to do is the exact same thing you do with your aura, which I believe the best term would be &quot;conceal&quot;. When you conceal or alter (terms used in M20) your aura with Mind or Prime, you are not really removing your aura or changing your condition and emotional state. You don't cease to be a mage just because you have &quot;changed&quot; you aura texture from sparkling to pale. You are just disguising it.<br /> <br /> Now, rule-wise, I believe that this effect should have the same system as concealing auras and mind shields. So, each success on the Arete roll would remove one success from anyone trying to scan for magickal effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 04-08-2025, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T06:37:07-07:00","id":1549940,"title":"","content":"Well, if it's like an aura. And there being magick to conceal auras. I think it makes sense to use the same system<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-08T09:53:44-07:00","id":1549948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549940#post1549940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if it's like an aura. And there being magick to conceal auras. I think it makes sense to use the same system</div> </div> </div> </div>Since M20 text about Resonance and Synergy does put those, Quintessence and auras in the same thing, they are all connected and definitely affect each other, possibly being just different sides of the same coin. But I'm not saying they are exactly the same, just that those are the default rules when you try to hide/scan for something. Mind shields works that way (iirc) and reading auras too.<br /> <br /> So it only makes sense to apply the same rule. Which means that if you want to cloak your spell on demand you don't have much chance to do. But if you're prepared, you could sneak some spells, unless the scanner also try extended rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T17:42:40-07:00","id":1549986,"title":"","content":"I think I have a better grasp of your question now.<br /> <br /> So here it is: Nightfolk do not detect Magic by default, don't worry about that.<br /> <br /> Only two splats can naturally detect supernatural effects just by them being supernatural: Changelings and Demons. They have other weaknesses, this sense for magic is one of their core advantages, and I doubt you'll use them as random mooks, so I both discourage stripping them of this and don't think it will be an issue.<br /> <br /> Resonance is (outside extreme cases) noticeable only through <i>Awareness</i>, and the availability in Mage's standard sheet undermines how <i><b>rare</b></i>this Talent is. Even Nightfolk won't have it, much less have it high, all that frequently.<br /> <br /> A more thorough note on the aspects that can be detected would be like that: <b>casting method</b> is whatever the Mage does to make the magic. It isn't the Instrument <i>per se</i>, but its actualization. If a Nightfolk enters the room and finds chalk runes all around and a bloody dagger in the center, it doesn't takes a lot to figure that something happened. Concealing it isn't rocket science, but I mention it because we always have to begin with the basics, or we end up forgetting them (and they're basics).<br /> <br /> The same goes for <b>direct effect</b>. One player of mine tried to do a concealed EXPLOSION spell once, without concealing the effect. It was an explosion. Effects may be noticeable in many different ways, specially in Mage (where you can give yourself many different senses), but otherwise are self-explanatory. If you want to conceal yourself, either cast an effect that isn't noticeable to begin with, or conceal the result in some appropriate way.<br /> <br /> We have already an understanding in <b>Resonance</b>. Yes, it is more noticeable, but it is also more rarefied. Even if someone with Awareness notices it, it actually has very little information on the spell. Concealing it is more about concealing <i><b>your traces</b></i> than concealing your Magic. It's up to you if &quot;regular&quot; Mages have access to the methods you found to conceal Resonance, and they all should work just fine, but in the end not concealing Resonance isn't that big of a deal. Usually it is only relevant for someone that already knows the Resonance of that specific Mage. I'd go as far as to suggest that only Nefandi should have read access to such concealment, because the Nightfolk is already too much at a disadvantage against Mages, specially as far as detection goes.<br /> <br /> By <b>Magic</b> I meant using an actual specified power to perceive the spell, and those are rare. Worse, they're usually bad at detecting specifics about the spell. The only splat that really detects Magic with ease and detail are <b>Demons</b>. Do with that what you may.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-09T19:33:30-07:00","id":1549990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549986#post1549986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So here it is: Nightfolk do not detect Magic by default, don't worry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about? Nightfolk have Awareness talent and disciplines gifts etc that allows them to detect supernatural stuff. But even without powers, Awareness is a talent, which means, in theory, that even without Awareness they could roll Perception to detect magick.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549986#post1549986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Nightfolk is already too much at a disadvantage against Mages, specially as far as detection goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree about the detection thing, but nightfolk are not in desvantage in M20 with that crazy counterspell rule\u2026<br /> <br /> Also, you are considering Resonance as the only thing they could detect in spells? (Besides casting methods and direct effect, which can be subtle in a low key spell).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T09:58:16-07:00","id":1550042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1549990#post1549990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, you are considering Resonance as the only thing they could detect in spells? (Besides casting methods and direct effect, which can be subtle in a low key spell).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, I admit I totally forgot that <i>Awareness</i>' description cites detecting Magic.<br /> <br /> The fact is, <i>Awareness</i> never got actual rules on how to do most of the things it is supposed to do. The only rule we have on the Core M20 is to detect Nightfolk, and it is almost useless given that it doesn't say when you can roll it or how to define the Diff, and even this rule calls for a Standard Action.<br /> <br /> We get rules on how to detect <i>Resonance</i> in the Book of Secrets, pp 129, and this rule is very clear that <i>Awareness </i>is kind of an exception to other Talents: you can only roll it without dots for <i>Resonance</i> 3 and above (which is <b>A LOT</b>, if you consider that level 5 is an obvious living storm that risks Disbelief just by existing).<br /> <br /> So, yeah, as I don't think that detecting Magic being easier than detecting <i>Resonance</i> makes any sense, and given that no rule ever actually made Magic detectable by <i>Awareness</i> alone, I indeed consider that <i>Awareness</i> can only detect <i>Resonance</i>, not the spell itself. And given your worries, I recommend you do the same. Detecting supernaturals in a very generic way and perceiving <i>Resonance</i> are already a lot for a Talent to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T11:04:47-07:00","id":1550047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1550042#post1550042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, I admit I totally forgot that <i>Awareness</i>' description cites detecting Magic.<br /> <br /> The fact is, <i>Awareness</i> never got actual rules on how to do most of the things it is supposed to do. The only rule we have on the Core M20 is to detect Nightfolk, and it is almost useless given that it doesn't say when you can roll it or how to define the Diff, and even this rule calls for a Standard Action.<br /> <br /> We get rules on how to detect <i>Resonance</i> in the Book of Secrets, pp 129, and this rule is very clear that <i>Awareness </i>is kind of an exception to other Talents: you can only roll it without dots for <i>Resonance</i> 3 and above (which is <b>A LOT</b>, if you consider that level 5 is an obvious living storm that risks Disbelief just by existing).<br /> <br /> So, yeah, as I don't think that detecting Magic being easier than detecting <i>Resonance</i> makes any sense, and given that no rule ever actually made Magic detectable by <i>Awareness</i> alone, I indeed consider that <i>Awareness</i> can only detect <i>Resonance</i>, not the spell itself. And given your worries, I recommend you do the same. Detecting supernaturals in a very generic way and perceiving <i>Resonance</i> are already a lot for a Talent to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iirc, awareness can be rolled reflexively by the ST or actively by the player. It has a lot of rules and applications but no due explanation of what exactly it does. It can be used to detect nightfolk, magick, auras. dodge attacks, detect Resonance. It's a fucking rank 1 sphere in a talent.<br /> <br /> Yeah. according to BoS p.129, it seems you shouldn't be able to roll awareness without dots in it, so why the fuck it's a talent? lol<br /> <br /> Awareness description in M20 has &quot;detect magick&quot; and &quot;recognize Resonance echoes&quot; among wht the talent can do. Do you consider those to be the same thing? Like, the only way to detect the use of magick is through Resonance?<br /> <br /> What about using Prime 1, would cloaking Resonance be enough to cloak your spell from a Prime 1 scan (considering you win a resisted roll)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T11:12:00-07:00","id":1550048,"title":"","content":"Well yes and no. The useful part of spheres is knowing what it does. Awareness cant tell you what it does only that it feels unnatural.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-11T11:49:56-07:00","id":1550052,"title":"","content":"So, yeah, <i>Awareness</i> is either a superpower or does very little, depending on how you take its description and many scattered suggestions seriously.<br /> <br /> In M20 it only gets mention in the Dramatic Systems section, in the table of sample rolls. There's just Detect Nightfolk, and is clearly cited as a Standard Action.<br /> <br /> Personally I play it loose as a &quot;detect what the ST wants you to detect&quot; ability, with a few caveats. If I don't call for it just because I want the players to notice, I'll let a character notice a Nightfolk if they spend the required Action. And I'll always let them notice <i>Resonance</i> that isn't cloaked through Magic, because that's what <i>Resonance</i> is mostly for, and because I like the premise of a Mage leaving a signature of sorts in their Magic.<br /> <br /> Using <b>Prime</b> Magic should reveal the spell regardless of <i>Resonance</i>, although it could certainly increase the amount of successes, or even the Diff, but by no more than 1 either. Even if it is a low level, it's Sphere Magic, and it is looking at the Tapestry, not at the <i>Resonance</i>. But concealing <i>Resonance</i> means (if we go with the above understanding) that the chance of the Mage who's looking for it even knowing where or what to look for are considerably reduced (and looking for Magic all the time, everywhere, isn't practical), and they won't know the identity of the caster, either (as this is perceived from the <i>Resonance</i> itself).<br /> <br /> Now, can a spell be made to read <i>Resonance</i>? That depends. Is the concealment really a concealment, or was the <i>Resonance</i> removed entirely? Does the spell look at it now, or at it in the moment of the casting? How was this <i>Resonance</i> concealed/removed? Here it pays to have both concealmente as a general rule and concealment as a work of Magic.<br /> <br /> To be sincere, I'm actually on the fence if <i>Resonance</i> should be easy to conceal or not, and I'm currently leaning towards only Nefandi knowing how to do it. But again, that's definitely me and my current chronicle (I need my PCs to be able to recognize the <i>Resonance</i> of the BBEGs, who are a cabal of powerful Marauders, but not notice that the nearby rival team are a bunch of Nefandi).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T09:17:10-07:00","id":1550073,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28439\" data-vbnamecard=\"28439\">quelsec</a> , well yeah, and I'm ok with spheres being able to do that. Spheres should be way more powerful than a talent. Also, sphere use requires an action and is not passive as awareness seems to be (at least in M20), which is only fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1550052#post1550052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, yeah, <i>Awareness</i> is either a superpower or does very little, depending on how you take its description and many scattered suggestions seriously.<br /> <br /> In M20 it only gets mention in the Dramatic Systems section, in the table of sample rolls. There's just Detect Nightfolk, and is clearly cited as a Standard Action.<br /> <br /> Personally I play it loose as a &quot;detect what the ST wants you to detect&quot; ability, with a few caveats. If I don't call for it just because I want the players to notice, I'll let a character notice a Nightfolk if they spend the required Action. And I'll always let them notice <i>Resonance</i> that isn't cloaked through Magic, because that's what <i>Resonance</i> is mostly for, and because I like the premise of a Mage leaving a signature of sorts in their Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, you don't use it as a passive ability. Now that I think about it, it was revised that had that passive thing for awareness and I couldn't find anything saying that it works passively. The only text about that is BoS description of of the ranks of Resonance, and it seems only strong Resonances can be passively felt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1550052#post1550052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using <b>Prime</b> Magic should reveal the spell regardless of <i>Resonance</i>, although it could certainly increase the amount of successes, or even the Diff, but by no more than 1 either. Even if it is a low level, it's Sphere Magic, and it is looking at the Tapestry, not at the <i>Resonance</i>. But concealing <i>Resonance</i> means (if we go with the above understanding) that the chance of the Mage who's looking for it even knowing where or what to look for are considerably reduced (and looking for Magic all the time, everywhere, isn't practical), and they won't know the identity of the caster, either (as this is perceived from the <i>Resonance</i> itself).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, concealing Resonance means that the mage scaning won't pick anything other than &quot;the Tapestry is weaving&quot;, so no emotion, no signature, no caster identity or any of that. And even that weaving could be concealed with Prime.<br /> <br /> While considering that it has to be an active, standard action, would indeed reduce the chance of detection (even for a non concealed spell), a mage/crat that sees something happening and wants to scan to know if the cause was magick (considering a coincident effect), could scan for that and that's where concealing with Prime would be good.<br /> <br /> If you start a fire in a room by forcing a short circuit in the electrical system, you should also hide the spell Resonance and Tapestry weaving to guarantee that it would be seen as a regular event.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549633-cloaking-resonance?p=1550052#post1550052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b<br /> Now, can a spell be made to read <i>Resonance</i>? That depends. Is the concealment really a concealment, or was the <i>Resonance</i> removed entirely? Does the spell look at it now, or at it in the moment of the casting? How was this <i>Resonance</i> concealed/removed? Here it pays to have both concealmente as a general rule and concealment as a work of Magic.<br /> <br /> To be sincere, I'm actually on the fence if <i>Resonance</i> should be easy to conceal or not, and I'm currently leaning towards only Nefandi knowing how to do it. But again, that's definitely me and my current chronicle (I need my PCs to be able to recognize the <i>Resonance</i> of the BBEGs, who are a cabal of powerful Marauders, but not notice that the nearby rival team are a bunch of Nefandi).</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are all good questions. BoS makes it pretty easy to conceal Resonance, unless it is a very strong one. While I really like the concept of Resonance (it gives a personal touch to the character), I think it should be easily concealed. Mages are already <b>very</b> good at investigation and detecting stuff, having a trail in all your spells makes it even worse.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Now, can a spell be made to read <i>Resonance</i>?\u200b</i><br /> <br /> Yes, Prime 1 and awareness can read Resonance. That's raw.<br /> <br /> <i>Is the concealment really a concealment, or was the <i>Resonance</i> removed entirely?\u200b</i><br /> <br /> Concealing requires Prime 2 while removing it requires Prime 4. So, I'd say that someone could try to read a concealed Resonance (in a resisted roll), but not a removed one. Afterall, it doesn't exist anymore.<br /> <br /> <i>Does the spell look at it now, or at it in the moment of the casting?</i><br /> <br /> That's a very interesting one. Could a mage with Time and Prime scan for a concealed spell before it was concealed? Well, I'd say that depends how the hiding was made. If the mage casted the spell and then concealed the Resonance/Tapestry(Quintessence), then I'd say yes.<br /> Now, if the mage hid the Resonance and made a previous spell that would hide the weaving of the Tapestry for his effects, than I'd say no.<br /> <br /> <i>How was this <i>Resonance</i> concealed/removed?\u200b</i><br /> <br /> Mechanically, with Prime 2 or 4 for concealing or removing, respectively.<br /> <br /> Story wise, it will greatly depend on the mage's paradigm, but I guess the base line is to make the Tapestry and Quintessence, or whatever he believes that Reality and magick is (Ether?), look like it haven't been manipulated.<br /> <br /> A good analogy would be that the Tapestry is like a canvas, Quintessence is the paint and magick is the painting. Hiding your spells would be like using underpainting technique or special sealant to blend your new brushstrokes perfectly into the original canvas.<br /> <br /> Or the Tapestry is like a grand symphony of reality, quintessence is the raw sound energy and vibrations and magick is like composing or remixing. Hiding the spell would be like subtly adding/editing the existing composition in a unnoticeable way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}